IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Internal Wiring) Regulations 2005 (S 479/2005), made under section 74 of the Act (section 97 in the 2020
-- Revised Edition), in operation 21 July 2005.  Text: TA1999-IW-S479-2005 under
-- subjects/sg/telecommunications-internal-wiring-regulations-2005/registers/source-bundle/.  It governs who may do telecommunication wiring
-- work between a user's equipment and the public licensee's interface point.  A date before 21 July 2005 answers NOTHING.

§ `IW regulations 1 and 2: citation and definitions`

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:50 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Internal Wiring)
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:51 | Regulations 2005 and shall come into operation on 21st July 2005.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:53 | Definitions
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:54 | 2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:55 | "Code of Practice" means the Code of Practice published by the Authority under
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:56 | regulation 4 (1);
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:57 | "interface point" means any point of interconnection between a user’s
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:58 | telecommunication equipment and any telecommunication system of a
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:59 | public telecommunication licensee;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:60 | "internal telecommunication wiring" means any telecommunication line, optical
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:61 | fibre, conduit or other physical medium connecting a user’s
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:62 | telecommunication equipment and any interface point but does not include
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:63 | the use of extension cords with built-in connectors and sockets;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:64 | "licence" means a telecommunication wiring contractor’s class licence granted
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:65 | under regulation 5 or a telecommunication wiring installer’s licence
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:66 | granted under regulation 6;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:67 | "licensee" means any person to whom a licence has been granted under these
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:68 | Regulations;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:69 | "telecommunication equipment" means any appliance, apparatus or accessory
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:70 | used or intended to be used for telecommunication;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:71 | "telecommunication wiring contractor" means any person who —
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:72 | (a) in the course of or in connection with or for the purposes of any trade
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:73 | or business carried on by him, performs or carries out any
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:74 | telecommunication wiring work or who offers to perform or carry out such
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:75 | work or who causes or arranges for such work to be performed or carried
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:76 | out; or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:77 | (b) for profit or reward, offers his services as a telecommunication wiring
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:78 | contractor;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:79 | "telecommunication wiring installer" means any person whose trade or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:80 | occupation requires or includes the personal performance by him of any
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:81 | telecommunication wiring work;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:82 | "telecommunication wiring work" includes the installation, maintenance or repair
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:83 | of a user’s internal telecommunication wiring;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:84 | "user" means a person who has subscribed to any telecommunication service of a
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:85 | public telecommunication licensee.
@ref IW regs 1 and 2 (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:50-85)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date (from 21 July 2005)` MEANS
    d AT LEAST (Date 21 7 2005)

GIVEN `it is a point of interconnection between a user's telecommunication equipment and a telecommunication system of a public telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 2: this is an "interface point"` MEANS
    `it is a point of interconnection between a user's telecommunication equipment and a telecommunication system of a public telecommunication licensee`

GIVEN `it is a telecommunication line, optical fibre, conduit or other physical medium connecting a user's telecommunication equipment and an interface point` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the use of extension cords with built-in connectors and sockets` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 2: this is "internal telecommunication wiring"` MEANS
    `it is a telecommunication line, optical fibre, conduit or other physical medium connecting a user's telecommunication equipment and an interface point` AND (NOT `it is the use of extension cords with built-in connectors and sockets`)

GIVEN `the person performs or offers or arranges telecommunication wiring work in the course of or in connection with a trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person offers his services as a telecommunication wiring contractor for profit or reward` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 2: the person is a "telecommunication wiring contractor"` MEANS
    `the person performs or offers or arranges telecommunication wiring work in the course of or in connection with a trade or business` OR `the person offers his services as a telecommunication wiring contractor for profit or reward`

GIVEN `the person's trade or occupation requires or includes the personal performance of telecommunication wiring work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 2: the person is a "telecommunication wiring installer"` MEANS
    `the person's trade or occupation requires or includes the personal performance of telecommunication wiring work`

GIVEN `the work is the installation, maintenance or repair of a user's internal telecommunication wiring` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 2: this is "telecommunication wiring work"` MEANS
    `the work is the installation, maintenance or repair of a user's internal telecommunication wiring`

GIVEN `the person has subscribed to a telecommunication service of a public telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 2: the person is a "user"` MEANS
    `the person has subscribed to a telecommunication service of a public telecommunication licensee`

GIVEN `it is a telecommunication wiring contractor's class licence granted under regulation 5 or a telecommunication wiring installer's licence granted under regulation 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 2: this is a "licence"` MEANS
    `it is a telecommunication wiring contractor's class licence granted under regulation 5 or a telecommunication wiring installer's licence granted under regulation 6`

GIVEN `it is any appliance, apparatus or accessory used or intended to be used for telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 2: this is "telecommunication equipment"` MEANS
    `it is any appliance, apparatus or accessory used or intended to be used for telecommunication`

GIVEN `it is the Code of Practice the Authority published under regulation 4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 2: this is the "Code of Practice"` MEANS
    `it is the Code of Practice the Authority published under regulation 4(1)`

GIVEN `the person was granted a licence under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 2: the person is a "licensee"` MEANS
    `the person was granted a licence under these Regulations`

§ `IW regulations 3 to 9`

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:90 | 3. The licensing authority in respect of every licence granted under these Regulations
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:91 | shall be the Authority with the consent of, or under the terms of a general authority given
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:92 | by, the Minister.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:94 | Code of Practice
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:95 | 4. —(1) The Authority shall publish a Code of Practice setting out the technical
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:96 | standards and specifications for the performance or carrying out of telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:97 | wiring work, which the Authority may, from time to time, modify.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:98 | (2) The Code of Practice may be made available to any person upon request and upon
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:99 | payment of the fee specified in the First Schedule.
@ref IW regs 3 and 4 (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:90-99)
GIVEN `the Authority acts with the Minister's consent or under a general authority from the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 3: the Authority is the licensing authority for the licence` MEANS
    `the Authority acts with the Minister's consent or under a general authority from the Minister`

GIVEN `the person requests the Code of Practice and pays the fee specified in the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 4(2): the Code of Practice is made available to the person` MEANS
    `the person requests the Code of Practice and pays the fee specified in the First Schedule`

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:102 | 5. —(1) Subject to regulation 8, no person other than a holder of a telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:103 | wiring contractor’s class licence shall —
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:104 | (a) act as a telecommunication wiring contractor;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:105 | (b) advertise, notify or state that he carries on or is willing to carry on the business
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:106 | of a telecommunication wiring contractor; or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:107 | (c) in any way hold himself out as ready to undertake for payment or other
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:108 | remuneration (whether monetary or otherwise) any of the functions of a
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:109 | telecommunication wiring contractor.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:110 | (2) A person shall be deemed to have been granted a telecommunication wiring
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:111 | contractor’s class licence if he has —
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:112 | (a) registered with the Authority in such form and manner as may be specified by
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:113 | the Authority;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:114 | (b) submitted to the Authority upon registration such information in writing as the
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:115 | Authority may require; and
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:116 | (c) paid to the Authority the fee specified in the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:117 | (3) A telecommunication wiring contractor’s class licensee shall —
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:118 | (a) comply with the conditions of class licence set out in the Second Schedule;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:119 | and
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:120 | (b) notify the Authority in writing of any change in any information furnished to
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:121 | the Authority under this regulation within 14 days of such change.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:122 | (4) The Authority may issue a written acknowledgment in such form as the Authority
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:123 | may determine to indicate that a telecommunication wiring contractor has been granted a
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:124 | telecommunication wiring contractor’s class licence in accordance with these
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:125 | Regulations.
@ref IW reg 5 (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:102-125)
GIVEN `the person holds a telecommunication wiring contractor's class licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person performs wiring work in premises of which he is the owner or occupier (regulation 8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts as, advertises or states that he is willing to act as, or holds himself out as ready for payment to act as, a telecommunication wiring contractor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 5(1): the person may act as a telecommunication wiring contractor` MEANS
    (NOT `the person acts as, advertises or states that he is willing to act as, or holds himself out as ready for payment to act as, a telecommunication wiring contractor`) OR `the person holds a telecommunication wiring contractor's class licence` OR `the person performs wiring work in premises of which he is the owner or occupier (regulation 8)`

GIVEN `the person registered with the Authority in the form and manner specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person submitted the information in writing that the Authority required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person paid the fee specified in the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 5(2): the person is deemed to have been granted a telecommunication wiring contractor's class licence` MEANS
    `the person registered with the Authority in the form and manner specified` AND `the person submitted the information in writing that the Authority required` AND `the person paid the fee specified in the First Schedule`

GIVEN `the class licensee complies with the conditions in the Second Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days after a change in the information furnished that the class licensee notified the Authority in writing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 5(3): the class licensee has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the class licensee complies with the conditions in the Second Schedule` AND (`days after a change in the information furnished that the class licensee notified the Authority in writing` AT MOST 14)

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:127 | 6. —(1) Subject to regulation 8, no person other than a holder of a telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:128 | wiring installer’s licence shall —
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:129 | (a) act as a telecommunication wiring installer;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:130 | (b) advertise, notify or state that he carries on or is willing to carry on the business
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:131 | of a telecommunication wiring installer; or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:132 | (c) in any way hold himself out as ready to undertake for payment or other
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:133 | remuneration (whether monetary or otherwise) any of the functions of a
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:134 | telecommunication wiring installer.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:135 | (2) An application for a telecommunication wiring installer’s licence shall be made to
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:136 | the Authority in such form and manner as the Authority may require and shall be
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:137 | accompanied by —
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:138 | (a) the appropriate fee specified in the First Schedule; and
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:139 | (b) such particulars, information and documents as the Authority may require.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:140 | (3) The Authority may refuse to grant an application for a telecommunication wiring
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:141 | installer’s licence if the Authority is not satisfied as to the educational qualification or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:142 | experience of the applicant, having regard to the nature of the duties of a
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:143 | telecommunication wiring installer.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:144 | (4) A telecommunication wiring installer’s licence shall be in such form as may be
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:145 | provided by the Authority and shall be subject to such conditions as the Authority may,
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:146 | from time to time, determine.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:147 | (5) The Authority may at any time, by notice in writing, vary all or any of the conditions
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:148 | upon which a telecommunication wiring installer’s licence is granted or impose
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:149 | additional conditions and the licensee shall, at his own expense, comply with the varied
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:150 | or additional conditions.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:151 | (6) A telecommunication wiring installer’s licensee shall notify the Authority in writing
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:152 | of any change in any information furnished to the Authority under this regulation or as
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:153 | specified in his licence within 14 days of such change.
@ref IW reg 6 (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:127-153)
GIVEN `the person holds a telecommunication wiring installer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person performs wiring work in premises of which he is the owner or occupier (regulation 8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts as, advertises or states that he is willing to act as, or holds himself out as ready for payment to act as, a telecommunication wiring installer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 6(1): the person may act as a telecommunication wiring installer` MEANS
    (NOT `the person acts as, advertises or states that he is willing to act as, or holds himself out as ready for payment to act as, a telecommunication wiring installer`) OR `the person holds a telecommunication wiring installer's licence` OR `the person performs wiring work in premises of which he is the owner or occupier (regulation 8)`

GIVEN `the application is in the form and manner the Authority required, with the fee in the First Schedule and the particulars, information and documents required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is not satisfied as to the educational qualification or experience of the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 6(2) and (3): the Authority may grant the telecommunication wiring installer's licence` MEANS
    `the application is in the form and manner the Authority required, with the fee in the First Schedule and the particulars, information and documents required` AND (NOT `the Authority is not satisfied as to the educational qualification or experience of the applicant`)

GIVEN `the licensee complies, at its own expense, with the conditions and any the Authority varied or added by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days after a change in the information furnished that the licensee notified the Authority in writing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 6(4) to (6): the licensee has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the licensee complies, at its own expense, with the conditions and any the Authority varied or added by written notice` AND (`days after a change in the information furnished that the licensee notified the Authority in writing` AT MOST 14)

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:156 | 7. A licence shall remain valid unless cancelled or suspended in accordance with the
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:157 | provisions of the Act or these Regulations.
@ref IW reg 7 (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:156-157)
GIVEN `the licence was cancelled or suspended in accordance with the Act or these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 7: the licence remains valid` MEANS
    (NOT `the licence was cancelled or suspended in accordance with the Act or these Regulations`)

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:160 | 8. —(1) Regulations 5 (1) and 6 (1) shall not apply to any person who performs or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:161 | carries out any telecommunication wiring work in any premises of which he is the owner
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:162 | or occupier.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:163 | (2) No owner or occupier of any premises shall perform or carry out any
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:164 | telecommunication wiring work in that premises unless such work is done in accordance
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:165 | with the Code of Practice.
@ref IW reg 8 (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:160-165)
GIVEN `the person is the owner or occupier of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 8(1): regulations 5(1) and 6(1) do not apply to the person's wiring work in the premises` MEANS
    `the person is the owner or occupier of the premises`

GIVEN `the wiring work in the owner's or occupier's premises is done in accordance with the Code of Practice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 8(2): the owner or occupier may perform the wiring work` MEANS
    `the wiring work in the owner's or occupier's premises is done in accordance with the Code of Practice`

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:167 | 9. A licensee shall not assign, transfer, sublet or otherwise dispose of the benefit of any
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:168 | licence granted under these Regulations, or permit another person to participate in any of
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:169 | the benefits, powers or authority granted under the licence except with the consent in
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:170 | writing of the Authority.
@ref IW reg 9 (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:167-170)
GIVEN `the licensee has the Authority's written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee assigns, transfers, sublets or otherwise disposes of the benefit of a licence, or permits another person to participate in its benefits, powers or authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 9: the licensee may do it` MEANS
    `the licensee has the Authority's written consent` OR (NOT `the licensee assigns, transfers, sublets or otherwise disposes of the benefit of a licence, or permits another person to participate in its benefits, powers or authority`)

§ `IW regulations 10 to 17`

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:173 | 10. —(1) If the Authority is satisfied that any licence has been lost, destroyed or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:174 | defaced, the Authority may, upon payment of the fee specified in the First Schedule,
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:175 | issue a replacement licence.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:176 | (2) No replacement licence shall be issued in place of a defaced licence unless the
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:177 | defaced licence is first surrendered to the Authority for cancellation.
@ref IW reg 10 (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:173-177)
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied the licence was lost, destroyed or defaced and the fee in the First Schedule is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence is defaced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defaced licence is first surrendered to the Authority for cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 10: the Authority may issue a replacement licence` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied the licence was lost, destroyed or defaced and the fee in the First Schedule is paid` AND ((NOT `the licence is defaced`) OR `the defaced licence is first surrendered to the Authority for cancellation`)

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:180 | 11. —(1) The Authority may, by notice in writing, cancel or suspend, for such period as
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:181 | it thinks fit, a licence if the licensee —
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:182 | (a) has performed or carried out any telecommunication wiring work otherwise
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:183 | than in accordance with the Code of Practice;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:184 | (b) has caused or allowed any telecommunication wiring work to be performed or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:185 | carried out by an unlicensed telecommunication wiring installer;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:186 | (c) has made, or caused, or allowed to be made or produced in or in connection
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:187 | with any application by him, or on his behalf, for a licence, any false, misleading
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:188 | or inaccurate information, whether in writing or not;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:189 | (d) has, in the opinion of the Authority, contravened any of the provisions of the
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:190 | Act or these Regulations or with any of the conditions of the licence;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:191 | (e) gives notice to the Authority in such form and manner as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:192 | determine that he has ceased to be a telecommunication wiring contractor or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:193 | telecommunication wiring installer, as the case may be;
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:194 | (f) has ceased to carry on any business or trade as a telecommunication wiring
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:195 | contractor or telecommunication wiring installer and his registration, if any, of the
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:196 | business under the Business Registration Act (Cap. 32) is cancelled; or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:197 | (g) being a company incorporated under the Companies Act (Cap. 50) or a limited
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:198 | liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:199 | (Act 5 of 2005), has gone into liquidation other than for the purpose of
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:200 | amalgamation or reconstruction.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:201 | (2) Upon the cancellation or during the period of suspension of any licence, the licensee
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:202 | shall for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations be deemed to be not licensed.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:203 | (3) The licensee whose licence is cancelled or suspended shall, if required by the
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:204 | Authority, surrender the licence to the Authority within such time as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:205 | specify.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:206 | (4) A licensee whose licence has been cancelled or suspended by the Authority, or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:207 | terminated at his own request, shall not be entitled to any compensation or refund of fees
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:208 | by the Authority in respect of the unexpired period of the licence.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:209 | (5) A cancellation of a telecommunication wiring contractor’s class licence of a person
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:210 | shall not operate so as to prevent such person from subsequently being deemed a holder
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:211 | of such a licence in accordance with regulation 5.
@ref IW reg 11 (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:180-211)
GIVEN `the licensee performed wiring work otherwise than in accordance with the Code of Practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee caused or allowed wiring work to be performed by an unlicensed telecommunication wiring installer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee made or allowed false, misleading or inaccurate information in an application for a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the Authority's opinion the licensee contravened the Act, these Regulations or a condition of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee gave notice that it has ceased to be a telecommunication wiring contractor or installer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee has ceased to carry on any business or trade as a contractor or installer and its registration under the Business Registration Act is cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee, a company or limited liability partnership, has gone into liquidation other than for amalgamation or reconstruction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 11(1): the Authority may by written notice cancel or suspend the licence` MEANS
        `the licensee performed wiring work otherwise than in accordance with the Code of Practice`
    OR `the licensee caused or allowed wiring work to be performed by an unlicensed telecommunication wiring installer`
    OR `the licensee made or allowed false, misleading or inaccurate information in an application for a licence`
    OR `in the Authority's opinion the licensee contravened the Act, these Regulations or a condition of the licence`
    OR `the licensee gave notice that it has ceased to be a telecommunication wiring contractor or installer`
    OR `the licensee has ceased to carry on any business or trade as a contractor or installer and its registration under the Business Registration Act is cancelled`
    OR `the licensee, a company or limited liability partnership, has gone into liquidation other than for amalgamation or reconstruction`

GIVEN `the licence is cancelled or during the period of suspension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 11(2): the licensee is deemed to be not licensed` MEANS
    `the licence is cancelled or during the period of suspension`

GIVEN `the Authority requires the licensee to surrender the licence within the time specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee surrenders it within that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 11(3): the licensee has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
    (NOT `the Authority requires the licensee to surrender the licence within the time specified`) OR `the licensee surrenders it within that time`

GIVEN `the licence was cancelled or suspended by the Authority, or terminated at the licensee's own request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 11(4): the licensee is entitled to compensation or a refund of fees for the unexpired period` MEANS
    FALSE

GIVEN `the licensee's class licence is cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 11(5): the cancellation prevents the person from subsequently being deemed a holder under regulation 5` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:214 | 12. —(1) The Authority may, at the request of any user, inspect the telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:215 | wiring work performed or carried out by a licensee to ensure that such work is in
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:216 | accordance with the Code of Practice.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:217 | (2) Upon inspection, the Authority may —
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:218 | (a) advise the user that the telecommunication wiring work has been carried out in
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:219 | accordance with the Code of Practice; or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:220 | (b) where any telecommunication wiring work has not been carried out in
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:221 | accordance with the Code of Practice, direct the licensee in writing to regularise,
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:222 | within such period as the Authority may determine and to its satisfaction, such
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:223 | telecommunication wiring work at his own expense.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:224 | (3) Any licensee who fails to comply with the directions issued by the Authority under
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:225 | paragraph (2) (b) shall be guilty of an offence.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:226 | (4) The Authority may impose the fee specified in the First Schedule for the second or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:227 | any subsequent inspection requested by the user under paragraph (1).
@ref IW reg 12 (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:214-227)
GIVEN `a user requested the Authority to inspect the wiring work performed by a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 12(1): the Authority may inspect the wiring work to ensure it is in accordance with the Code of Practice` MEANS
    `a user requested the Authority to inspect the wiring work performed by a licensee`

GIVEN `the work has been carried out in accordance with the Code of Practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee complies with the Authority's written direction to regularise the work within the period and to its satisfaction, at his own expense` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 12(2) and (3): the licensee is not guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the work has been carried out in accordance with the Code of Practice` OR `the licensee complies with the Authority's written direction to regularise the work within the period and to its satisfaction, at his own expense`

GIVEN `this is the second or a subsequent inspection requested by the user` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`IW reg 12(4): the fee in dollars the Authority may impose` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `this is the second or a subsequent inspection requested by the user` THEN JUST 70 OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:230 | 13. —(1) The Authority may, from time to time, cause the names of all persons who
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:231 | hold valid licences and such other information as the Authority thinks fit to be entered in
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:232 | a register kept for that purpose.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:233 | (2) The Authority may make available the list of licensees to any person upon request.
@ref IW reg 13 (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:230-233)
GIVEN `the person holds a valid licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 13: the Authority may enter the person's name in the register and make the list of licensees available on request` MEANS
    `the person holds a valid licence`

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:237 | 14. A licensee may, with the approval of the Authority, cease or refuse to perform or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:238 | carry out any telecommunication wiring work for any user if he is of the opinion that —
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:239 | (a) the user's internal telecommunication wiring is not in accordance with the
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:240 | Code of Practice; or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:241 | (b) such telecommunication wiring work is likely to threaten the safety or proper
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:242 | functioning of any telecommunication system of a public telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:243 | licensee.
@ref IW reg 14 (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:237-243)
GIVEN `the Authority approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee is of the opinion that the user's internal wiring is not in accordance with the Code of Practice, or the work is likely to threaten the safety or proper functioning of a public telecommunication licensee's system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 14: the licensee may cease or refuse to perform the wiring work for the user` MEANS
    `the Authority approved` AND `the licensee is of the opinion that the user's internal wiring is not in accordance with the Code of Practice, or the work is likely to threaten the safety or proper functioning of a public telecommunication licensee's system`

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:248 | 15. Any person who contravenes any of the provisions of these Regulations shall be
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:249 | guilty of an offence.
@ref IW reg 15 (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:248-249)
GIVEN `the person contravenes any provision of these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 15: the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person contravenes any provision of these Regulations`

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:252 | 16. The Authority may, in its discretion —
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:253 | (a) waive all or any conditions in any licence; and
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:254 | (b) subject to such conditions as it thinks fit, waive or reduce the payment of the
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:255 | fee payable for a licence.
@ref IW reg 16 (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:252-255)
GIVEN `the Authority waives the condition, or waives or reduces the fee on conditions it thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 16: the condition or fee does not apply, or applies as reduced` MEANS
    `the Authority waives the condition, or waives or reduces the fee on conditions it thinks fit`

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:258 | 17. —(1) The Telecommunication (Internal Wiring) Regulations (Rg 9) are revoked.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:259 | (2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), any licence granted under the revoked
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:260 | Telecommunication (Internal Wiring) Regulations shall, unless revoked, cancelled or
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:261 | suspended, and in so far as it is not inconsistent with these Regulations —
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:262 | (a) continue and be deemed to be a licence under these Regulations; and
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:263 | (b) be subject to the terms and conditions specified in the Second Schedule.
@ref IW reg 17 (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:258-263)
GIVEN `the licence was granted under the revoked Telecommunication (Internal Wiring) Regulations (Rg 9)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence has been revoked, cancelled or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW reg 17(2): the licence continues as a licence under these Regulations, on the terms of the Second Schedule` MEANS
    `the licence was granted under the revoked Telecommunication (Internal Wiring) Regulations (Rg 9)` AND (NOT `the licence has been revoked, cancelled or suspended`)

§ `IW Schedules`

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:271 | 1. For each copy of the Code of Practice $10
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:272 | 2. For a telecommunication wiring contractor’s class licence $100
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:273 | 3. For a telecommunication wiring installer’s licence $30
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:274 | 4. For each replacement of a telecommunication wiring installer’s licence $5
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:275 | 5. For a second or any subsequent inspection by the Authority under $70.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:276 | regulation 12 (4)
@ref IW First Schedule (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:271-276)
GIVEN item IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`IW First Schedule: the fee in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF item EQUALS 1 THEN JUST 10
           IF item EQUALS 2 THEN JUST 100
           IF item EQUALS 3 THEN JUST 30
           IF item EQUALS 4 THEN JUST 5
           IF item EQUALS 5 THEN JUST 70
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:284 | 1. The holder of a telecommunication wiring contractor’s class licence (referred to in
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:285 | this Schedule as the class licensee) shall at all times have in his employment a
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:286 | telecommunication wiring installer who holds a valid telecommunication wiring
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:287 | installer’s licence.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:288 | 2. The class licensee shall ensure that only a holder of a valid telecommunication wiring
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:289 | installer’s licence carries out any telecommunication wiring works in the course of the
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:290 | class licensee’s trade or business.
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:291 | 3. The class licensee shall comply with the provisions of the Act, these Regulations and
-- src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:292 | any code of practice issued under the Act.
@ref IW Second Schedule (src:TA1999-IW-S479-2005:284-292)
GIVEN `the class licensee has at all times in its employment a telecommunication wiring installer who holds a valid licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `only holders of a valid telecommunication wiring installer's licence carry out telecommunication wiring works in the course of the class licensee's trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the class licensee complies with the Act, these Regulations and any code of practice issued under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IW Second Schedule items 1 to 3: the class licensee is meeting the conditions` MEANS
    `the class licensee has at all times in its employment a telecommunication wiring installer who holds a valid licence`
    AND `only holders of a valid telecommunication wiring installer's licence carry out telecommunication wiring works in the course of the class licensee's trade or business`
    AND `the class licensee complies with the Act, these Regulations and any code of practice issued under the Act`
